 1. Executive Summary
SpeakFill lets a person fill a long, formal form by simply talking. The user speaks once, in Urdu, Roman Urdu or English. The system transcribes the speech, extracts structured values with a single AI call, validates them locally (CNIC, phone, email, dates), asks only for what is missing, and produces a clean, print-ready PDF that supports Urdu script.
In Pakistan, forms for banks, universities, employers and public offices are mostly in English, long, and unforgiving about formatting. Millions of people either cannot read them confidently or cannot type quickly in English. SpeakFill removes both barriers while keeping the user in control through a mandatory review step.
Key differentiators
•	Local-first language support: Urdu script, Roman Urdu and code-mixed speech; Pakistani formats (CNIC 13 digits, 03xx phone, day-first dates) are native.
•	Cost-efficient AI: A full form costs 1 to 2 LLM calls, not one per field. Deterministic rules run before the model, and repeat inputs are served from cache.
•	Trust by design: Every value is colour-coded by confidence, nothing is invented, and the user confirms before a PDF is created.
•	Resilient: Provider chain (Gemini, then Groq, then rules-only) plus an offline demo mode, so the product never hard-fails.
2. Problem Statement
Form-filling is a high-friction, high-stakes task. A single mistake (a wrong CNIC digit or date format) can cause rejection, repeat visits, or paying a middleman.
Pain point	Impact
Language barrier	Forms are in English; many users think and speak in Urdu or a regional language.
Typing barrier	Typing Urdu or long English addresses on a phone is slow and error-prone.
Format strictness	CNIC, phone and date formats are validated manually by staff; errors cause rejection.
Dependence on middlemen	Users pay typists or cyber cafes and share private data (CNIC, address) with strangers.
Existing AI tools	General chatbots do not output a validated, formatted form, and are costly or inconsistent for Urdu.
Note: market sizing figures are intentionally not stated here as facts. Before external distribution, validate them with a source (see Section 17, Open Questions).
3. Vision, Goals and Non-Goals
Vision: Every person can complete any official form in their own language, in minutes, without a middleman.
Product goals
•	G1. Reduce time to complete a 13-field form from roughly 10 to 15 minutes (manual) to under 3 minutes.
•	G2. Achieve at least 90% field-level accuracy after review for supported forms (target, to be measured in user testing).
•	G3. Keep AI cost at or below 2 LLM calls per completed form.
•	G4. Remain fully usable on free-tier API quotas and degrade gracefully when quotas run out.
Non-goals (this release)
•	Uploading arbitrary PDFs or scanned forms and auto-detecting fields (OCR). Planned for Phase 2.
•	Direct submission to banks, universities or government portals.
•	User accounts, payments and long-term storage of personal data.
•	Native mobile apps (responsive web works on mobile browsers).
4. Target Users and Personas
Persona	Profile	Needs
Ayesha, 22 Fresh graduate	Urban, comfortable speaking English/Urdu mix, applying to many jobs and universities.	Speed; repeat forms without retyping; clean PDF.
Muhammad Aslam, 48 Small shopkeeper	Fluent in Urdu, limited English reading, wants to open a bank account.	Voice only; Urdu labels; confidence he is not making mistakes.
Rukhsana, 35 First-time applicant	Regional language speaker (Punjabi/Pashto/Sindhi), limited digital literacy.	Guided, one-question-at-a-time mode; very simple screens.
Cyber cafe / help desk operator	Fills forms for walk-in customers all day.	Throughput; multi-form support; accuracy.
5. User Stories
ID	As a ... I want ... so that ...	Priority
US-1	As an applicant, I want to speak all my details in one go so that I do not have to type.	Must
US-2	As a user, I want to speak in Urdu, Roman Urdu or English so that I can use my natural language.	Must
US-3	As a user, I want to see which fields the AI is unsure about so that I can fix them quickly.	Must
US-4	As a user, I want the app to ask only for missing fields so that I do not repeat myself.	Must
US-5	As a user, I want to download a clean PDF (with Urdu text rendered correctly) so that I can print or submit it.	Must
US-6	As a low-literacy user, I want a guided mode with one question at a time so that I am not overwhelmed.	Should
US-7	As a user, I want to fix any field by voice or keyboard so that I stay in control.	Should
US-8	As a presenter, I want an offline demo so that the product works without internet.	Should
6. Scope and Release Plan
Phase	Scope	Status
MVP (v2.0)	Voice dictation + guided mode, 4 built-in forms, AI extraction, local validation, clarification loop, Urdu PDF, usage counter, offline demo, cloud deployment	Built; 10 automated tests passing
Phase 2 (0 to 3 months)	PDF/image upload with OCR and field detection, form builder UI, saved profile (opt-in), more forms (NADRA, passport, utility, scholarship)	Planned
Phase 3 (3 to 9 months)	Mobile apps, WhatsApp bot, organisation dashboard, REST API and embeddable widget, more languages	Planned
Phase 4 (9+ months)	Direct integrations with institutions, e-signature, analytics, enterprise SSO	Vision
